# Project-level Claude Code settings. Both are maintainer/machine workflow preferences,
# not part of the package a cloner installs, so neither ships. settings.json here carries
# worktree.bgIsolation, which relaxes a background-session safety guard — imposing that on
# anyone who clones this repo would be wrong.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# SubagentStop ledger — one line per worker completion, regenerated by the hook every
# run. It is machine-local worker history, not shared project history worth diffing like
# source. See docs/DESIGN-RATIONALE.md for the fuller design rationale.
.claude/worker-ledger.jsonl

# Git worktrees created for isolated worker runs (isolation: worktree).
.claude/worktrees/

# Agent project-memory. Ignored *in this repository only*. This repo is the distributable
# package, not a codebase a team works in, so one author's session notes would ship to
# every cloner rather than serve a team working this codebase day to day. Onboarded
# projects keep this directory TRACKED instead — see orchestration-onboard/SKILL.md step 5
# and docs/DESIGN-RATIONALE.md for why this repository's own exception is explicit and
# documented rather than drift.
.claude/agent-memory/
